{{also|other-worldly}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|otherworld|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|ŭ''th'''ər-wûrldʹli|a=US}}, {{IPA|en|/ˌʌðɚˈwɝld.li/}}
{{rfap|en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, concerned with, or [[preoccupy|preoccupied]] with a different world than that of the [[tangible]] [[here and now]], such as a [[heavenly]], [[spiritual]], or [[imaginary]] world.
#: {{syn|en|ethereal|mystical|transcendental}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1917|author=[[w:H._G._Wells|H. G. Wells]]|title=God, the Invisible King|chapter=5
|passage=Every religion that becomes ascendant, in so far as it is not '''otherworldly''', must necessarily set its stamp upon the methods and administration of the law.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=26 Aug 2007|author=Clive Davis|url=http://entertainment.timesonline.co.uk/tol/arts_and_entertainment/music/cd_reviews/article2310136.ece|title=Simphiwe Dana: The One Love Movement on Bantu Biko Street|work=Times of London|passage=Dana has the '''otherworldly''' temperament of a mystic.}}
# Not belonging to the [[real]] world; [[unnatural]]; [[odd]] and [[unfamiliar]].
#: {{syn|en|alien}}
#* {{RQ:Galsworthy Saint's Progress|chapter=VII|section=1|page=285|passage=He had not seen cricket played since the war began; it seemed almost '''other-worldly''', with the click of the bats, and the shrill young voices, under the distant drone of that sky-hornet threshing along to Hendon.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Jonathan Martin|title=For a Clinton, It’s Not Hard to Be Humble in an Effort to Regain Power|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2015/04/16/us/politics/you-dont-have-to-tell-a-clinton-twice.html?_r=0|work=w:The New York Times|date=15 April 2015
|passage=An almost '''otherworldly''' resilience has characterized the 40-year arc of the Clintons’ political lives, a well-documented pattern of dazzling success, shattering setback and inevitable recovery.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Scenes from New York City as Ida paralyzes region|date=2021-09-01|work=The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/02/nyregion/flash-floods-new-york.html|issn=0362-4331|author=Michael Levenson; Anne Barnard|passage=The sudden inundation from the remnants of Ida transformed familiar scenes of life in New York into '''otherworldly''' and waterlogged chaos on Wednesday night.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Sarfraz Manzoor|quotee=Suzi Ronson|title=‘Bowie said he’d sell his soul to be famous’: Suzi Ronson on sex, ruthless ambition – and dyeing David’s hair red|work=The Guardian|date=2024-04-02|url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2024/apr/02/david-bowie-suzi-ronson-sex-ambition-dyeing-ziggy-stardust|issn=0261-3077|passage=“David used to say he would sell his soul to be famous,” she says. “But he was also '''otherworldly''' – and you couldn’t take your eyes off him.”}}

